  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Building in Migration and Border Management in Guinea (CBMBM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of the project is to promote state and human security in Guinea by supporting law enforcement agencies to be more effective, accountable, and inclusive. Up to 4 border posts will be renovated or built and equipped with radios in the targeted areas. Through a series of capacity building activities, law enforcement agents will be trained to detect fraudulent travel documents, identify suspicious cases, and aware of the need to protect migrants. A comprehensive border assessment will be produced. Data and information on cross-border migration will be collected and analyzed by the border posts equipped with advanced data collecting system such as the Migration Information Data Analysis System and the installation of Flow Monitoring Points. Border agents will receive several trainings on data collection, use of data protection and privacy. The Government of Guinea will have increased capacity to collect, manage and analyse information on cross-border movement and develop evidence-based migration policies, as well as capacities to adapt their work to the COVID-19 context.</narrative>
  </description>
